stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "pending_verification" as pending_verification
    state "active" as active
    state "expiring_soon" as expiring_soon
    state "frozen" as frozen
    state "expired" as expired

    [*] --> active: purchase or confirmed VNPay [eligible] / create active membership
    pending_verification --> active: lifecycle sync [verified and >7 days] / persist active
    pending_verification --> expiring_soon: lifecycle sync [verified and <=7 days] / persist expiring_soon
    pending_verification --> frozen: lifecycle sync [verified and freeze window active] / persist frozen
    pending_verification --> expired: lifecycle sync [verified and expiry passed] / persist expired
    active --> pending_verification: lifecycle sync [email unverified] / persist pending_verification
    expiring_soon --> pending_verification: lifecycle sync [email unverified] / persist pending_verification
    frozen --> pending_verification: lifecycle sync [email unverified] / persist pending_verification
    expired --> pending_verification: lifecycle sync [email unverified] / persist pending_verification

    note bottom of pending_verification
        Derived by derive_membership_status when the account is unverified.
        The FSM permits inbound reconciliation from active, expiring_soon,
        frozen, and expired; the scheduled lifecycle sync persists it.
    end note
    note bottom of active
        Verification reconciliation excludes cancelled and revoked because
        both terminal states are immutable during lifecycle synchronization.
    end note
